  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "I2C on the Nano 33 IoT: SDA = A4, SCL = A5. SCL (A5) of reader and writer are joined on bb1 strip 10t; SDA (A4) of both are joined on bb1 strip 12t. GND of the two boards is wired directly together, as in the image.",
   "Pull-up network: 4.7k r1 from SCL to the 3V3 rail and 4.7k r2 from SDA to the 3V3 rail, as in the image. The 3V3 rail is on bb2 (tp.1 and tp.2 are the same rail strip), fed from the reader's 3V3 pin. The 3V3 rail is used (not 5V) because the board is 3.3 V logic.",
   "The manual lists 2 mini breadboards and 10 jumper wires but the image shows neither breadboards nor the exact wire layout. I assumed bb1 carries the I2C bus and bb2 carries the pull-ups and 3V3 rail; the extra 4 jumper wires are the bus-to-pull-up links and pull-up-to-rail links. Exact hole positions are my choice.",
   "The boards are not shown seated in a breadboard in the image, so wires go from the board header pins to breadboard holes.",
   "Each board is powered and programmed over its own USB cable from the computer. The computer is not a graph part, so the USB cables only connect to the boards' USB ports."
  ]
 },
